<http://data.silknow.org/object/0f518633-d169-344c-abd6-2c35bb92851e/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Wall panel made of canvas and embroidered with wool, silk and silk chenille in tent, Hungarian, stem and canvas stitches with laid and couched work. The ground is covered with silver gilt thread laid and couched in whorls. A series of motifs - genre scenes, portraits, vases, statues, still life, etc. - is surrounded by exotic foliage comparable to that found on contemporary French bizarre silk designs. The genre figures are after tapestry designs by Teniers. The statue in the top left corner is after the Versailles garden statue, Air by Le Hongre (1683) and the figure on the lower right is similar to a second Versailles statue, the Venus de Richelieu."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0f518633-d169-344c-abd6-2c35bb92851e> .

